Third-party components
======================

The Flatpak bundle published with each release contains a complete build of
Wine -- its loader, its libraries, the patched kernel drivers (hidclass.sys,
winebus.sys and wineusb.sys, with the libusb half wineusb.so) and the patched
user-mode DLLs, all under /app.

These are NOT original works of this repository. They are compiled from the
Wine source tree with the patches in patches/ applied, and are therefore
derivative works of Wine, licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License
version 2.1 or later (LGPL-2.1-or-later).

  Upstream source : https://dl.winehq.org/wine/source/
  Version         : see WINE_VERSION
  Modifications   : every patch in patches/
  Rebuild         : flatpak-builder with
                    flatpak/io.github.adds39939.SynapseLinux.yml

The complete corresponding source is the upstream Wine tarball for the version
named in WINE_VERSION -- which the manifest downloads by URL and verifies by
sha256 -- plus the patches in patches/. The manifest is the build recipe, so it
and this repository together reproduce the binaries exactly.

The bundle also contains cabextract (GPL-2.0-or-later) and winetricks
(LGPL-2.1-or-later), both built from source by the same manifest, from the URLs
and revisions it pins.

A copy of the LGPL-2.1 is available at:
  https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/lgpl-2.1.txt

This project ships no Razer code or assets. Razer Synapse is proprietary
software; Razer's installer is downloaded from Razer by the application on first
run, and Synapse is installed from it. "Razer" and "Synapse" are trademarks of
their owner; this project is unaffiliated with and unendorsed by Razer. The
application icon is original to this project.

Microsoft's core fonts and .NET Framework 4.8 are likewise not shipped. They are
downloaded on first run by winetricks, in their original redistributable form:
Chromium cannot render without real fonts, and Razer's installer is a .NET
Framework application.
